                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TLDR:  A Space themed 1v1 MOBA with a unique style of resource management.  As of the time of writing this review the game is 100% Free to Play with absolutely no Pay to Win. Currently in Basic form, but still very enjoyable.\n\nIt's basically a 1v1 MOBA as of now, but what sets it apart is the style of resource management.  You take control of and build rings around planets which will in turn produce more units to go into your wave of minions.  There are also side objectives that spawn and can be contested over.     \n\nYour mothership will level up as the game progresses first unlocking the abilities you've chosen before the game, and then upgrading your ship itself (speed, attack speed, attack damage, hull, shield, something else i can't think of.)\n\nThere is more detail to go into about the production part (and hell all of it) but i don't truly understand it all yet.  Despite being in basic form, there are still abilities to experiment with and strategies to test.\n    \nThere are slow periods during the PvP and frantic bursts of micro management.   Not alot of ships or abilities to choose from yet but if the developers give this game some love, time, polish, and content It could really turn into something great.\n\n-AI is pretty simple, more of the tutorial than the ACTUAL tutorial(which doesn't cover much) \n-Has a nice space theme that for some reason reminds me of Homeworld (though the two have little in common) \n-Playerbase isn't much yet but it has to start somewhere.\n-You are starting with the same pool of ships/abilities to choose from as everyone else.  (LEVEL PLAYING FIELD!)  \n    \n It does look like when they add more ships/abilities/skins you will be able to unlock them with ingame currency earned through playing or probably buy it with real money.  If new content is balanced, this shouldn't become a problem.   \n\nAll in all  I'm having fun, I think other people will enjoy this game too.  I really recommend giving it a shot.\n\nAlso there's a parallel queue, so if you don't want to sit around waiting for a match you can beat up on some AI and the game will let you know when your match is ready.   \n\n\n\n",
